# Two identical DragonRise arcade encoders (VID:PID 0079:0006) report a zero GUID
# and the same name, so nothing distinguishes them but the physical USB port.
# Pin a stable, human-readable symlink to each port so the sticks are always
# identifiable (for diagnostics and any path-addressable tooling):
#
#   dragonrise-p1 = port 1-2  (controller xhci-hcd.0)
#   dragonrise-p2 = port 3-2  (controller xhci-hcd.1)
#
# NOTE: RetroArch (udev joypad driver) and SDL/ES-DE do NOT order pads by these
# symlinks — the symlinks are for diagnostics only. RetroArch orders by libudev
# syspath sort, which is fixed by physical port: port 1-2 (1f00200000.usb) sorts
# before port 3-2 (1f00300000.usb). The labels above are assigned to match that
# order, so whichever stick is plugged into port 1-2 is Player 1. controllers.yml
# no longer pins input_playerN_joypad_index (a fixed pin left Player 1 with no
# device when only one stick was connected), so port position is the only thing
# that decides player order. To swap players, swap the USB ports.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="js[0-9]*", ENV{ID_PATH}=="platform-xhci-hcd.0-usb-0:2:1.0", SYMLINK+="input/dragonrise-p1", GROUP="input", MODE="0660"
SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="js[0-9]*", ENV{ID_PATH}=="platform-xhci-hcd.1-usb-0:2:1.0", SYMLINK+="input/dragonrise-p2", GROUP="input", MODE="0660"
